WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.560
When it comes to the ongoing anthology&nbsp;
series American Horror Story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.480
the amount of twists and turns and&nbsp;
time-traveling can get a little confusing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.720
So, we're here to help you make sense of&nbsp;
the entire American Horror Story timeline.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.480
In the first season, Murder House, we learn that&nbsp;
famous Hollywood surgeon Dr. Charles Montgomery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.200
built a classic Los Angeles Victorian mansion&nbsp;
for his wife, Nora, while they were flush with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.560
celebrity money. But their fortune quickly turned&nbsp;
sour as Charles' mental illness and Frankenstein&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.360
complex forced him to give basement abortions&nbsp;
to make ends meet. The husband of one client&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.160
killed Charles and Nora's son in retaliation,&nbsp;
cutting him up into pieces. Charles stitched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.120
boy back together, along with other peoples'&nbsp;
parts, creating the monstrous Infantata.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.520
Was it this grotesque series of acts that&nbsp;
turned the Montgomery House evil? Or was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.160
the evil there all along? This question&nbsp;
has yet to be answered, but when Ben,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.360
Vivien, and Violet Harmon move into the haunted&nbsp;
mansion in 2011, it's been home to dozens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.080
suspicious deaths. It's not long before the&nbsp;
Harmons realize the ghosts of those people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.320
are very much active within the house's&nbsp;
walls, including their housekeeper Moira,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.760
who appears to Ben as a seductive young woman&nbsp;
and to Vivien as a sad but helpful older woman.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.400
And as if that wasn't enough for the poor&nbsp;
Harmons, Constance, Tate, and Addie Langdon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.640
are nosy next door neighbors who constantly&nbsp;
appear in their house without invitation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.520
and they only hint at the house's sordid&nbsp;
past without mentioning their own role in it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.400
Plus, Tate is having therapy sessions with Ben,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.040
and he and Violet quietly begin falling in&nbsp;
love until a new series of tragedies strike.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.280
Ben has been unfaithful to Vivien in the past,&nbsp;
so when he shows up in a kinky black rubber suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.920
Vivien thinks he's trying to rekindle the&nbsp;
previous passion of their marriage. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.440
it isn't Ben in the suit. The so-called "Rubber&nbsp;
Man" is actually Tate Langdon. And worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.680
the Harmons find out that Tate is another of&nbsp;
the ghosts haunting the house, having killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.720
himself on the property after committing a mass&nbsp;
shooting at school. Creepier still, after getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.080
it on with a ghost, Vivien is suddenly pregnant&nbsp;
with twins, one of whom is decidedly not human.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.080
"I'm sure you're aware that these babies, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.440
rather, one of these babies, has&nbsp;
been developing at a rapid rate."

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.640
The human child is stillborn, and the&nbsp;
other is revealed to be the Antichrist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.880
born from spirit and flesh as prophesied&nbsp;
by the psychic Billie Dean Howard.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.200
The hits for the Harmons don't stop there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.760
Tate convinces Violet to overdose on sleeping&nbsp;
pills so they can be together forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:33.200
She and her parents don't realize she's dead until&nbsp;
she tries to escape Murder House and can't leave.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.720
We then learn that Tate had hidden&nbsp;
her dead body underneath the house.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.760
Sadly, Vivien dies during childbirth, a birth&nbsp;
overseen by the ghost of Charles Montgomery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.960
and she becomes a new addition to the house. She&nbsp;
tells Ben to take the surviving child and escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.320
but the ghost of Ben's lover, Hayden, kills him&nbsp;
before he can. Constance Langdon takes the baby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.840
her grandson, instead. Of course,&nbsp;
there are no happy endings here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:00.640
as the first season of American Horror Story&nbsp;
ends three years later, with Constance finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.720
that her infant grandson has brutally killed&nbsp;
his nanny and is playing with her blood.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:12.480
Set mostly in 1964, second season Asylum starts&nbsp;
off with Kit Walker, a man who's kidnapped by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.200
aliens. After his wife and friend disappear,&nbsp;
Kit is imprisoned in Briarcliffe Manor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:21.840
an asylum for the criminally insane where the&nbsp;
staff are more disturbed than their patients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:26.080
Headed by Sister Jude, Briarcliffe is a&nbsp;
religious institution that handles its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.240
vulnerable patients with more torture than&nbsp;
care. Many of the patients aren't even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:35.600
criminals they've been painted to be, like Pepper,&nbsp;
a gentle, non-verbal, microcephalic woman falsely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.400
accused of killing a baby, as well as promiscuous&nbsp;
Shelley, whose husband locked her up for cheating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.600
On the medical staff are Dr. Oliver Thredson, in&nbsp;
charge of counseling, and the sadistic Dr. Arden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.920
a Nazi doctor who's performing horrific&nbsp;
experiments on Briarcliffe residents.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.960
Meanwhile, Lana Winters is a young gay journalist&nbsp;
who's been searching for her big break.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.040
Since lesbianism was considered a mental&nbsp;
illness at the time, Lana gets herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.920
committed to Briarcliffe to produce an&nbsp;
exposé about its gruesome ongoing events.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.360
She discovers that Dr. Thredson is Bloody Face —&nbsp;
a serial killer who's been sexually assaulting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.320
skinning, and decapitating women — after he&nbsp;
drugs and kidnaps her. However, she's his only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:20.400
surviving victim. Why? Because she's pregnant&nbsp;
with his baby. Lana's story shocks America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.273
after she exposes Briarcliffe and Thredson,&nbsp;
but years later, we find out that a Bloody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.273 --> 00:04:30.280
Face copycat who's been killing people at an&nbsp;
abandoned Briarcliffe is Lana and Thredson's son.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:36.160
In the third season, Coven, New Orleans is home&nbsp;
to Miss Robichaux's Academy for Exceptional Young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.600
Ladies, a boarding school for witches run by the&nbsp;
Supreme witch, Fiona Goode. Fiona has superpowers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.000
that she wields for her own narcissistic&nbsp;
ends, rather than the good of her community.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.520
Unfortunately for Fiona, signs emerge that a new&nbsp;
Supreme is on the rise as Fiona's health and looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:56.720
begin failing. There can only be one Supreme at a&nbsp;
time, and the old Supreme must die for the new one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.760
to take the mantle. The most promising Supreme&nbsp;
candidates at Robichaux's include timid Zoe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:07.120
confident Queenie, self-involved Madison&nbsp;
Montgomery, and sweet Nan, until Misty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.720
Day — an almost-killed swamp witch with a penchant&nbsp;
for Stevie Nicks — takes sanctuary in the Academy.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:18.000
In the meantime, a group of witch hunters led&nbsp;
by Hank Foxx, husband of Robichaux headmistress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.720
Cordelia Goode, is killing the new crop of&nbsp;
witches on their way to enroll at Robichaux's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.320
Old battle lines open anew when&nbsp;
Fiona approaches her nemesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:32.080
voodoo queen Marie Laveau, to find out the secret&nbsp;
of immortality so she can remain Supreme forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.720
When Marie refuses, Fiona releases the&nbsp;
serial killer and torturer of slaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.720
Delphine LaLaurie, that Marie had&nbsp;
under her spell, wreaking new havoc.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.000
As Fiona's powers wane, the&nbsp;
witches perform a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.840
tests called the Seven Wonders to see&nbsp;
who will ascend the Supreme throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:53.120
Ultimately, Cordelia passes all seven tests,&nbsp;
resurrecting Zoe who died during hers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.760
Misty Day ends up trapped in purgatory, and&nbsp;
Madison's narcissism gets her sent to Hell.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:03.840
American Horror Story's fourth season, Freak Show,&nbsp;
keeps us in the South, in the town of Jupiter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:10.320
Florida, during 1952. Elsa Mars and her Cabinet&nbsp;
of Curiosities run a waning lakeside carnival in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:15.520
a quiet town that loudly resents their presence.&nbsp;
The era of television is at its pinnacle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.440
and people would rather sit at home watching&nbsp;
the screen than the antics of freaks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.280
Lobster Boy Jimmy Darling, Ethel the Bearded Lady,&nbsp;
strongman Dell Toledo and his hermaphrodite wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:30.720
Desiree Dupree. To drum up sales, Elsa goes&nbsp;
on a hunt for new monsters to join her troupe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.840
finding the wholesome conjoined&nbsp;
twins Bette and Dot Tattler.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.880
However, Elsa's job gets even harder when serial&nbsp;
killer Twisty the Clown goes on a rampage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.880
leading townsfolk to think the carnies&nbsp;
were responsible for the gruesome murders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.520
More threats to the freaks emerge with shady&nbsp;
Stanley, who's buying and killing circus folks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:53.120
to sell their bodies to a medical marvel museum.&nbsp;
Worse, a rich psychopath named Dandy Mott becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:57.760
fixated on Bette and Dot, an obsession that&nbsp;
leads to him going on a killing spree that leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.800
most of Elsa's performers dead. Fortunately,&nbsp;
Bette, Dot, and Jimmy escape and get married.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.400
And for the first time, the show&nbsp;
makes direct references to another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.560
American Horror Story season, as&nbsp;
microcephalic Pepper from Asylum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.840
appears and reveals how her sister killed her&nbsp;
own malformed child and framed Pepper. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:21.480
we learn that Elsa's legs were amputated in a&nbsp;
snuff film by Asylum's villainous Nazi, Dr. Arden.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:27.520
Inspired by one of the most famous serial&nbsp;
killers in American history, H.H. Holmes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:33.360
the fifth season, Hotel, takes place in James&nbsp;
March's Hotel Cortez in downtown Los Angeles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:39.120
In 1922, March builds his hotel with a series&nbsp;
of secret walls and basements so he can kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.000
and dispose of guests without anyone noticing.&nbsp;
March is also in love with a young actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:48.720
Elizabeth, whose affections belong to&nbsp;
movie star Rudolph Valentino. So naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:54.880
March disposes of Valentino, but not before&nbsp;
Valentino turns Elizabeth into a vampire like him.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.320
After March's death, he leaves&nbsp;
the Cortez to Elizabeth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.480
now known as the Countess, who&nbsp;
remains its owner until 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:07.520
when she's forced to sell to fashion designer&nbsp;
Will Drake. The Countess plans to marry Drake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:12.560
and kill him to get her hotel back, but the&nbsp;
Cortez's ghosts — as well as other angry parties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:17.200
like her transgender bartender, Liz Taylor —&nbsp;
throw wrench after wrench into her bloody plans.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.960
"No pity party in my bar!"

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:25.440
All the while, a serial killer is brutalizing&nbsp;
people based on violations of the Ten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.480
Commandments. Detective John Lowe suspects the&nbsp;
killer is working from the hotel. Because he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.040
on the rocks with his wife, Alex, Lowe rents a&nbsp;
room to investigate. However, over the course of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:40.080
the series, we learn that March had been searching&nbsp;
for a protégé for years, and by the end of Hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:45.120
we discover that Detective Lowe is the Ten&nbsp;
Commandments Killer. Alex has also become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:50.080
vampire, and the Countess entrusts all the&nbsp;
vampire children in the Cortez to her care.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.840
We should also point out that Hotel has a&nbsp;
reference to the first season of American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:58.080
Horror Story, as the Countess goes to the&nbsp;
Montgomery House to get an abortion. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.640
the malformed vamp-baby lives,&nbsp;
and she tends to it to this day.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:08.640
Playing on its own narrative tricks, sixth season&nbsp;
Roanoke explores the real-life disappearance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:14.160
16th century North American settlers through&nbsp;
an in-show documentary entitled My Roanoke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.880
Nightmare — which centers around the testimony&nbsp;
of homeowners Shelby and Matt Miller, who buy a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:24.160
rundown mansion in the North Carolina woods and&nbsp;
experience supernatural terrors. They chalk it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:29.120
up to the inbred Polk Family who previously&nbsp;
owned the house. Matt's sister, Lee Harris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:33.920
comes with her young daughter Flora to help out,&nbsp;
and they all discover there are dark spirits not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:39.360
just in the house, but also in the woods, and life&nbsp;
in their fixer-upper becomes a fight for survival.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.800
My Roanoke Nightmare is the show&nbsp;
within the show that explores the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:48.320
Roanoke events featuring the folks who&nbsp;
lived it from 2014 through to 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:53.120
along with reenactors to play Shelby and&nbsp;
Matt, as well as Matt's sister, Lee Harris.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:58.160
The meta-commentary goes even deeper when My&nbsp;
Roanoke Nightmare producers decide to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.720
the real-life Shelby and company along with&nbsp;
the actors playing them back to the mansion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:07.200
during the Blood Moon. The Blood Moon is the&nbsp;
time when the ghosts of the area come alive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.720
and perform a series of violent rituals headed&nbsp;
by the "first lady" of Roanoke, Thomasin White,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:19.280
aka the Butcher. The original Supreme, Scáthach,&nbsp;
also manifests, ultimately possessing Lee Harris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:24.320
who proceeds to go on her own killing spree. To&nbsp;
save her daughter, Lee chooses to go with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:28.960
Roanoke ghosts, and the historical mystery&nbsp;
of the area only becomes more enigmatic.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.800
American Horror Story's seventh season, Cult,&nbsp;
drops us into the suburb of Brookfield Heights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:39.040
Michigan, in the wake of Donald&nbsp;
Trump's inauguration in 2017.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:44.480
Ally and her wife Ivy own a local restaurant&nbsp;
that's newly struggling due to divisive political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:49.440
rhetoric that's led to a rise in hate crimes&nbsp;
against marginalized people in their town.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:54.160
As a result, Ally's childhood traumas are&nbsp;
so severely provoked that her phobia of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:59.200
clowns emerges with a vengeance, as well as a&nbsp;
serious paranoia that someone's out to get her.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:03.920
Ally is far from wrong. A charismatic&nbsp;
but deeply bigoted and misogynistic man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:06.560
named Kai Anderson feels empowered by the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.800
political regime and runs for public&nbsp;
office on an open platform of hate.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.400
"I said there is nothing more dangerous&nbsp;
in this world than a humiliated man."

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.960
He's also the leader of a cult&nbsp;
that has been dressing up as clowns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.600
and killing people around town. But because&nbsp;
nobody but Ally has witnessed the clowns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:31.200
these murders get chalked up to a variety of other&nbsp;
motives. Ally's past mental health issues make her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:36.480
easy to gaslight when her wife comes out as one of&nbsp;
Kai's cult members. But in one of the more complex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:42.080
narrative seasons with numerous plotlines woven&nbsp;
together, it turns out that Kai's sexist platform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:48.240
was orchestrated by Valerie Solanas and her lover,&nbsp;
Bebe, in order to blast women out of complacency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:54.000
and into political rage. Solanas, famous for&nbsp;
shooting Andy Warhol, is also revealed to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:59.760
infamous Zodiac Killer who was never caught. After&nbsp;
Kai is killed, Ally runs for senate and wins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:03.760
ending the season with the suggestion that&nbsp;
she's become a new cult leader herself.

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:10.240
In the eighth season, Apocalypse, we learn that&nbsp;
Vivien Harmon and Tate Langdon's baby from Murder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:15.360
House is Michael Langdon, and he's the Antichrist,&nbsp;
here to kickstart the end times. But first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:20.560
the Hawthorne School for Exceptional Young Men —&nbsp;
the warlock version of Miss Robichaux's Academy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:25.680
in Coven — mistakes him for the most powerful&nbsp;
warlock ever known, one that might be the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:31.600
male to ascend to Supreme status. Michael passes&nbsp;
all of the Seven Wonders, and he even manages to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:37.440
rescue Misty Day, Madison Montgomery, and Queenie&nbsp;
from their purgatories. In the years after Coven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:41.440
Queenie visited the Hotel Cortez and&nbsp;
has been trapped there ever since.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:45.600
The actual Supreme, Cordelia Goode,&nbsp;
is doubtful about Michael's powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.720
but when her own begin to wane, she wonders if&nbsp;
it's true he's next in line of succession. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:56.400
is not. And by the time the witches figure it out,&nbsp;
Michael has instigated nuclear war on a devastated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:01.600
planet. But he was unable to kill all the witches,&nbsp;
and now, they're the only ones who can stop him.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:06.240
Cloaked under an identity spell in Outpost 3&nbsp;
— the former site of Hawthorne School — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.960
witch Mallory is the up-and-coming Supreme,&nbsp;
whose powers almost match that of Michael's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.080
She's able to travel through time to 2015&nbsp;
and kill Michael before he properly comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:21.760
into his Antichrist abilities, halting the&nbsp;
apocalypse. Or so we think. Apocalypse closes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:27.520
in an unspecified present where former Outpost&nbsp;
3 members Emily and Timothy meet, fall in love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:32.880
and have a baby. Like Baby Michael at the end of&nbsp;
Murder House, their child also kills the nanny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.160
suggesting that the birth of Satan&nbsp;
might not have been halted at all.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:42.000
We also think it's necessary to highlight a&nbsp;
particular episode directed by American Horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:46.720
Story queen Sarah Paulson, where we are taken&nbsp;
all the way back to the beginning to fill in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:52.240
number of pending storylines. Following the witch&nbsp;
Madison Montgomery and warlock Behold Chablis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:57.120
the episode finds the Montgomery House in&nbsp;
a sad state. Upon discovering her grandson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.800
was the Antichrist, Constance Langdon&nbsp;
killed herself there so she could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:05.280
with all the ghost children in the haunted&nbsp;
mansion, including the Infantata "monster."

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:09.840
The Harmons have retreated to their own&nbsp;
corners, with Vivien avoiding Ben at all cost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:14.640
and Violet refusing to have anything to do with&nbsp;
Tate Langdon, the boy she loved but who assaulted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:19.280
and impregnated her mom with the Antichrist.&nbsp;
Thanks to Madison and Behold's meddling, they find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:24.240
out the evil that had possessed Tate transferred&nbsp;
to Michael Langdon, and Madison helps Violet and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:28.960
Tate reconcile, which is another strange and&nbsp;
rare happy ending in American Horror Story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:34.160
Madison also helps the housekeeper Moira — who&nbsp;
Constance killed decades before after Moira had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.160
an affair with her husband — find her bones&nbsp;
and then be buried with her beloved mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:42.400
finally letting her rest in peace. Now&nbsp;
that the witches own the Montgomery House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.120
there should be no new ghosts&nbsp;
created within its walls.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:51.600
As is the case with many time travel narratives,&nbsp;
an entire plot arc can sometimes get dismantled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:57.120
as the story moves between different realities and&nbsp;
potentially parallel universes. When Mallory uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:03.360
her power to alter time itself by going back to&nbsp;
2015 and killing Satan's son, it raises one big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:08.000
unanswered question: How could time travel&nbsp;
affect the show's timeline as it stands?

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.720
Well, based on the years in which they take&nbsp;
place, the present-day events of Roanoke and Cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.600
might not have happened at all anymore. Of course,&nbsp;
the histories of the original Supreme, Thomasin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:22.320
the Butcher, the Polk family, and real-life Matt&nbsp;
and Shelby buying the mansion could be retained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:27.280
as well as the flashbacks to Valerie Solanas&nbsp;
and Andy Warhol in Cult. But what stands of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:32.000
the rest of these seasons is unclear until&nbsp;
we get more information in future episodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:37.360
Might the election results of Cult even shift in a&nbsp;
world where a first apocalypse was nearly averted?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:41.040
Or since a new Antichrist gets born&nbsp;
regardless, will the timelines play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.360
out similarly to how they already have?&nbsp;
We can only hope new seasons will tell.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:51.600
In many ways, the ninth season, 1984, was&nbsp;
something of a palate cleanser for fans of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:56.480
the show due to its standalone nature as a&nbsp;
mostly straightforward slasher movie homage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:01.600
Following a group of familiar American Horror&nbsp;
Story faces in new roles at Camp Redwood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:07.520
1984 dove big into '80s nostalgia through the&nbsp;
secrets of Camp Blood and all of its many ghosts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:12.960
new and old. Eagle-eyed fans spotted many&nbsp;
references in 1984 that called out or back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:17.840
previous seasons of the show. From small details&nbsp;
— like Margaret Booth buying Briarcliffe Manor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:22.960
from second season Asylum and the fact that&nbsp;
Mr. Jingles' cabin in Alaska is the same as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:28.080
Kit Walker's in Asylum — to massive thematic&nbsp;
connections like haunted places where the dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:32.560
don't stay dead starting all the way back&nbsp;
in the show's opening season Murder House.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:38.880
But arguably the biggest connection 1984 has to&nbsp;
the bigger arc of the narrative is its connection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:44.400
to Satan and his minions on Earth, a thread&nbsp;
that, thanks to Apocalypse, Coven, and Hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:49.680
has become one of the fundamental pillars of&nbsp;
the entire American Horror Story tapestry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:55.920
In 1984 we once again meet the Night Stalker&nbsp;
Richard Ramirez as he forges new deals with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:00.320
master Lucifer as well as other dangerous&nbsp;
killer ghosts. Because we don't exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:05.360
know how 1984 fits in with the changed world&nbsp;
brought about by Apocalypse yet, all we can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:10.720
is wait for future seasons of the anthology to&nbsp;
hopefully reveal more about the larger picture.

